In two weeks.

250
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:43,060
I see.

251
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:49,190
Well, I wish you both a lifetime of happiness.

252
00:17:49,980 --> 00:17:52,320
So you're bald.

253
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:54,150
Wait, wait.

254
00:17:56,740 --> 00:17:59,280
We'd really love it if you could be there.

255
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:03,030
Really?

256
00:18:04,910 --> 00:18:07,120
I know it would make me happy...

257
00:18:08,330 --> 00:18:09,830
...ma'am.

258
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:15,000
Then I wouldn't miss it for the world.

259
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:19,010
Oh, I'm getting all misty here. Ha!

260
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:22,220
You'd think I was having my legs waxed or something.

261
00:18:26,890 --> 00:18:29,690
- You okay?     - Yeah.

262
00:18:29,850 --> 00:18:32,150
Thanks for making me do this.

263
00:18:33,110 --> 00:18:37,240
Before we go on with the show, I want to say to the bride and groom...

264
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:40,320
...how lucky they are to have found each other.

265
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:44,080
In every life a little rain must fall.

266
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,620
Fortunately...

267
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:47,790
...in my life...

268
00:19:02,550 --> 00:19:06,010
When I was growing up, I played the one on the far left.

269
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:19,440
Remind me to introduce you to someone.

270
00:19:19,610 --> 00:19:21,150
- Who?     - Fourth gear.

271
00:19:24,990 --> 00:19:26,030
What?

272
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:28,450
What does he want? I wasn't doing anything.

273
00:19:28,620 --> 00:19:33,330
Maybe he saw your hands slip briefly from the 10 and 2:00 position.

274
00:19:35,630 --> 00:19:40,050
Maybe it's, uh, Sergeant Sagittarius coming back to flirt some more.

275
00:19:42,970 --> 00:19:44,260
It's a different guy.

276
00:19:47,390 --> 00:19:51,100
- Good evening, officer.     - Do you know how fast you were going?

277
00:19:51,310 --> 00:19:55,100
Uh, no, I don't, but it could not have been more than 60.

278
00:19:55,270 --> 00:19:57,060
You're right. It was 37.

279
00:20:02,030 --> 00:20:05,280
You're not ticketing me for driving too slow, are you?

280
00:20:05,490 --> 00:20:07,200
That's right.

281
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:17,630
You know, officer, I, uh...

282
00:20:19,130 --> 00:20:21,550
I had the weirdest dream last night.

283
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,970
Oh, my God!

284
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,010
Your license, please.

285
00:20:27,680 --> 00:20:31,020
You don't want to hear about my dream...

286
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:32,770
...Officer...

287
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:34,350
...Pretty?

288
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:39,520
It's Petty.

289
00:20:41,110 --> 00:20:43,570
I'll be right back with your ticket.

290
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:49,200
- You have a son.      - I know. I know.

291
00:20:55,250 --> 00:20:58,420
- Feel better?     - Yeah. Much. Heh.

292
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:00,250
Listen, uh...

293
00:21:00,420 --> 00:21:05,760
Not that I'm insecure about my manhood or anything, but, uh...

294
00:21:05,930 --> 00:21:08,680
...I need to hook up with a woman right now.

295
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:12,010
- I understand.     - Yeah, okay.

296
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:18,650
- Hey. Hi.     - Hi.

297
00:21:18,810 --> 00:21:21,400
You look familiar. Do I know you?

298
00:21:21,570 --> 00:21:22,900
I don't think so.

299
00:21:23,070 --> 00:21:25,490
Maybe it's because I'm on television.

300
00:21:27,610 --> 00:21:31,490
- I'm an actor on Days ofour Lives.      - Wow. Really?

301
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:34,500
- Four-fifty, please.      - Oh, let me get this.

302
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:46,720
These are for you.

